popularity... in other words, _after_ the most recent release (3.4.3).
As such, I do not think any of us can predict anything at ALL about the
Dev Team's attitude towards farming.

As further evidence, 3.4.3 was released on January 8, 2004.  The
earliest game recorded on nethack.alt.org started on March 27, 2002.

The top 9 scores on nethack.alt.org are all over 1,000,000,000 points;
all but one were started in 2005 or later, and that one was started in
early 2004.  The top 34 scores are all over 100,000,000 points; all but
five were started in 2005 or later, and one of those is DeathOnaStick's
polypiling-gems game (started in early 2004, finished in early 2005).

Now, certainly not all these games were a result of pudding farming,
though it is known for a fact that some, at least were.  However, it is
immediately obvious that no significant pudding farming was occurring
prior to the release of 3.4.3... leaving us all completely in the dark
regarding what, if anything, the Dev Team intends to do about this
(relatively) new problem.

